{"id":"n5-090","title":"だれ～","romaji":"dare～","jlptLevel":5,"shortExplanation":"Asking 'who' in a sentence, used to inquire about someone's identity or to clarify who is being referred to.","longExplanation":"The だれ〜 grammar point is used to ask about the identity of someone in a sentence. It can be translated as 'who' or 'whom' in English. It is often used with the particle が, は, or を, but can also be combined with other particles depending on the context.","formation":"だれ + appropriate particle (が, は or を)","examples":[{"jp":"だれがその本を買いましたか。","romaji":"Dare ga sono hon o kaimashita ka.","en":"Who bought that book?","words":[{"surface":"だれ","vocabId":"1416830","reading":"だれ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"その","vocabId":null},{"surface":"本","vocabId":"1522150","reading":"ほん"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"買い","vocabId":"1636070","reading":"かい","baseForm":"買う"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"だれを待っていますか。","romaji":"Dare o matteimasu ka.","en":"Whom are you waiting for?","words":[{"surface":"だれ","vocabId":"1416830","reading":"だれ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"待っ","vocabId":"1410590","reading":"まつ","baseForm":"待つ"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":"1158500","reading":"い","baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[0]},{"jp":"だれがそのリンゴを食べましたか。","romaji":"Dare ga sono ringo o tabemashita ka.","en":"Who ate that apple?","words":[{"surface":"だれ","vocabId":"1416830","reading":"だれ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"その","vocabId":null},{"surface":"リンゴ","vocabId":"1555480","reading":"りんご"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"食べ","vocabId":"1358280","reading":"たべる","baseForm":"食べる"},{"surface":"まし","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"